"section":10,"section_title":"Compressed generators and adaptive alphabets","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:b48c6ec8591c430733f6d326bbe98a619250b533e933d9c21ce7d6464efa8fe3","file":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/09-adaptive-alphabets.tex","line":28,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"08da65984689d78a9e30b827448f92b8882fcd8071c75c77c8c7f80200882198","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/09-adaptive-alphabets.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:b48c6ec8591c430733f6d326bbe98a619250b533e933d9c21ce7d6464efa8fe3","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Routing-densities-and-representation-contraction-for-Thorp-sweeps-September-26-2026/build/sections/09-adaptive-alphabets.tex#L28"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{rec:adaptive-main}\nThere are absolute positive constants $c,c',C$ such that for every\ndyadic $n$ and every partition $\\lambda=(n-r,\\rho)\\vdash n$,\n\\begin{align}\n \\|F_n|_{V_\\lambda}\\|_{\\op}&\\le e^{-c h_n(r)},\n       \\label{rec:generator-level-main}\\\\\n \\Tr_{V_\\lambda}F_n^4&\\le\n       \\exp\\{-c'\\log D_\\lambda+C h_n(r)\\}.\n       \\label{rec:adaptive-trace-main}\n\\end{align}\nConsequently $\\|T_n|_{V_\\lambda}\\|_{\\op}$ is at most\n$\\exp[-c_0\\{\\log D_\\lambda+h_n(r)\\}]$ for an absolute $c_0>0$."}
